{"tool_name":"crh","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"CRH","home":"https://github.com/UCLOrengoGroup/cath-tools","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"cath-resolve-hits (CRH)- tool that resolves domain matches suspiciously quickly.","addition_date":"2019-07-04T17:24:08Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T21:07:26.854862Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Suite"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:CRH","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"name":"Ian Sillitoe","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://sillit.com/"},{"name":"Tony E Lewis","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://github.com/tonyelewis"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://cath-tools.readthedocs.io/en/latest/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Fold recognition","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0303"},{"term":"Sequence trimming","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3192"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"CRH","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"Ruta","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/bty863","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: Many bioinformatics areas require us to assign domain matches onto stretches of a query protein. Starting with a set of candidate matches, we want to identify the optimal subset that has limited/no overlap between matches. This may be further complicated by discontinuous domains in the input data. Existing tools are increasingly facing very large data-sets for which they require prohibitive amounts of CPU-time and memory. Results: We present cath-resolve-hits (CRH), a new tool that uses a dynamic-programming algorithm implemented in open-source C++ to handle large datasets quickly (up to 1 million hits/second) and in reasonable amounts of memory. It accepts multiple input formats and provides its output in plain text, JSON or graphical HTML. We describe a benchmark against an existing algorithm, which shows CRH delivers very similar or slightly improved results and very much improved CPU/memory performance on large datasets.","authors":[{"name":"Lees J.G."},{"name":"Lewis T.E."},{"name":"Sillitoe I."}],"citationCount":19,"date":"2019-05-15T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"Cath-resolve-hits: A new tool that resolves domain matches suspiciously quickly"},"pmcid":"PMC6513158","pmid":"30295745","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Protein folds and structural domains","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0736"},{"term":"Sequence sites, features and motifs","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0160"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"CRH","home":"https://bio.tools/CRH","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"cath-resolve-hits (CRH)- tool that resolves domain matches suspiciously quickly.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:crh/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":true,"registration":false},"packages":true,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":false,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":23,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2020"},{"count":2,"year":"2025"},{"count":2,"year":"2026"},{"count":3,"year":"2024"},{"count":4,"year":"2021"},{"count":5,"year":"2022"},{"count":6,"year":"2023"}],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/bty863","pmcid":"PMC6513158","pmid":"30295745","ref_count":7,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"2010"},{"count":1,"year":"2011"},{"count":1,"year":"2012"},{"count":1,"year":"2015"},{"count":1,"year":"2018"},{"count":2,"year":"2016"}],"title":"cath-resolve-hits: a new tool that resolves domain matches suspiciousl